tgs:RevisionEvent.DefinedInPass_2026_10_18 a thinkr:RevisionEvent ;
    thinkr:revisionDate "2026-10-18"^^xsd:date ;
    thinkr:revisionKind thinkr:RevisionKindType.InitialBuild ;
    thinkr:revisionNote "thinkr:definedIn pass over the 165 works, reviewed by MJSullivan (judgment-call pairs skipped). Added thinkr:definedIn for 24 concept-work pairs where the work is the idea's origin text (thinkr:definedIn tgs:Work.LimitsToGrowth1972 was added just before), added an analytical lens to the 17 of them that had none (Intellectology left untagged, since no lens fits), and minted tgs:Concept.GameTheory, tgs:Concept.NonZeroSumness and tgs:Concept.ProgressTrap with their origin works. tgs:Concept.GameTheoryFillsTheOughtGap and tgs:Concept.PositiveSumInGroupNegativeSumToNature now relatesTo the new concepts. Caveats kept with two pairs: the idea of energy additions is older than York and Bell (2019), whose paper names it; Boehm's 'reverse dominance hierarchy' dates from a 1993 paper that Hierarchy in the Forest (1999) develops. Rejected pairs (work cited but not the origin) stay as dcterms:source or prose; the Indicator links to the California Doughnut report stay dcterms:source. A work's lens is derived by query through thinkr:definedIn, not asserted on the work."@en ;
    .

