tgs:RevisionEvent.Frankly_106_DuplicateResolution a thinkr:RevisionEvent ;
    thinkr:affects tgs:Monologue.Frankly_106_TenThingsWorthMoreThanAPoundOfGold ;
    thinkr:revisionDate "2026-09-12"^^xsd:date ;
    thinkr:revisionKind thinkr:RevisionKindType.Correction ;
    thinkr:revisionNote "Real, genuine pre-existing duplicate discovered during the TGS/RR/Frankly merge: this episode had been independently, fully built twice in the original episodes.ttl under two slightly different real IRI names (this one, and the now-retired Frankly_106_TenThingsWorthMoreThanGold) -- predates all of this session's batch-pilot work; not something the merge process itself created, only what it caught. Resolved by keeping the more complete of the two (this one carries a real, formal dct:references property the other only had in prose) and discarding the other entirely."@en ;
    .

tgs:RevisionEvent.EvolvingDoughnut2025_Added a thinkr:RevisionEvent ;
    thinkr:affects tgs:SchoolOfThought.DoughnutEconomics, tgs:Work.TheEvolvingDoughnut2025, tgs:Work.DoughnutOfSocialAndPlanetaryBoundaries2025, thinkr:IndicatorCategory ;
    thinkr:revisionDate "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    thinkr:revisionKind thinkr:RevisionKindType.InitialBuild ;
    thinkr:revisionNote "Brought Doughnut Economics up to Doughnut 3.0 from MJSullivan's upload of Raworth's 'The Evolving Doughnut' (DEAL, October 2025). Minted four Works (Doughnut 1.0 Oxfam paper 2012, Doughnut 2.0 Lancet Planetary Health article 2017, Doughnut 3.0 Nature article 2025, and the explainer itself) and tgs:Human.AndrewFanning; added the version history and 3.0 dimension names to tgs:SchoolOfThought.DoughnutEconomics; attached the 3.0 dimension names as CloseMatch alternate terms on seven IndicatorCategory individuals whose California labels differ. Global 2021-22 indicator values not recorded; the 42 Indicators stay California's."@en ;
    .

tgs:RevisionEvent.WorldInTransition2026_Added a thinkr:RevisionEvent ;
    thinkr:affects tgs:Work.WorldInTransition2026, tgs:Organization.EarthkindCollective ;
    thinkr:revisionDate "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    thinkr:revisionKind thinkr:RevisionKindType.InitialBuild ;
    thinkr:revisionNote "Added the Earthkind Collective report 'World in Transition: Strategic Responses to the Metacrisis' (2026) and its author organization, from a PDF MJSullivan downloaded via Hylo. dct:references to the 17 existing works it cites or recommends, with back-links; dct:relation to Metacrisis, MultipolarTrap and LeveragePoints."@en ;
    .

tgs:RevisionEvent.BioregioningEarthInitiatives_Import a thinkr:RevisionEvent ;
    thinkr:affects tgs:Work.BioregioningEarthOntology, thinkr:Initiative, thinkr:PracticeTerm, thinkr:PracticeCluster ;
    thinkr:revisionDate "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    thinkr:revisionKind thinkr:RevisionKindType.InitialBuild ;
    thinkr:revisionNote "Imported all ten Bioregioning Earth cluster pages from PDFs MJSullivan printed (five first, the other five the same day), for use as real-world examples in WWNS. New schema: thinkr:Initiative, thinkr:PracticeTerm, thinkr:PracticeCluster, thinkr:carriedOutBy, thinkr:hasPracticeTerm, thinkr:listedInPracticeCluster, thinkr:placeName. New data (initiatives.ttl): 10 clusters, 69 practice terms, 221 initiatives; 52 organizations added to organizations.ttl. The site's 'Finance Assesments' is labeled 'Finance Assessments'. The practice-term to InterventionSubdomain crosswalk (skos:relatedMatch) is Claude's draft; 9 terms have no match. Organization places are given only where the page text or well-known facts support them; three are left blank (ASPROCIG, Landschaftspflegeverein, Mira River Guardians). An earlier web-reader pass had paired several examples with the wrong organization; the PDF text was parsed directly and is correct."@en ;
    .

tgs:RevisionEvent.OrganismEarthTranscript_Linked a thinkr:RevisionEvent ;
    thinkr:affects tgs:Series.GreatSimplificationAnimatedSeries ;
    thinkr:revisionDate "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    thinkr:revisionKind thinkr:RevisionKindType.InitialBuild ;
    thinkr:revisionNote "Linked the Organism.earth library's transcript of the 2022 animated film to tgs:Series.GreatSimplificationAnimatedSeries (rdfs:seeAlso plus a note), at MJSullivan's request. The page is a transcript of a work already in the graph, so no new Work was minted. The site's authors list was noted as a possible future source of thinkers but could not be fetched."@en ;
    .

tgs:RevisionEvent.OrganismEarthLibrary_Added a thinkr:RevisionEvent ;
    thinkr:affects tgs:Work.OrganismEarthLibrary ;
    thinkr:revisionDate "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    thinkr:revisionKind thinkr:RevisionKindType.InitialBuild ;
    thinkr:revisionNote "Added the Organism.earth library as a reference work, from MJSullivan's PDF of its author list (352 names). MJSullivan's framing: a resource for later, not a list to copy. No people were added. A match of the list against the graph found 23 authors already present and 10 TGS guests; Riane Eisler (TGS 116) is a guest with no Human yet because that episode is still a stub."@en ;
    .

tgs:RevisionEvent.OppositionModeling_Added a thinkr:RevisionEvent ;
    thinkr:affects thinkr:OppositionType, thinkr:challenges, tgs:SchoolOfThought.TechnoOptimism ;
    thinkr:revisionDate "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    thinkr:revisionKind thinkr:RevisionKindType.InitialBuild ;
    thinkr:revisionNote "Added opposition modeling at MJSullivan's request, for vetting papers in WWNS, after reviewing a Gemini summary of opposing movements. New: thinkr:OppositionType (CompetingParadigm, FriendlyCritique, OrganizedDoubt), thinkr:challenges, thinkr:hasOppositionType; six schools (EffectiveAccelerationism, Ecomodernism, Cornucopianism, NeoclassicalGrowthEconomics, Ecosocialism, OrganizedClimateDoubt); five works; three humans (Andreessen, Simon, Oreskes); ExxonMobil; six challenges links each with LinkNote and Candidate Evidence. Deliberately not added from the Gemini text: Musk, Thiel, Luckey and Verdon (investment is not a stated position; add only with their own public statements), AEI and Cato (its citations did not support the funding claims), and degrowth or ecosocialism as opposition (friendly critics; their critique awaits a citable source)."@en ;
    .

tgs:RevisionEvent.RedTeamBridges_2026_10_19 a thinkr:RevisionEvent ;
    thinkr:affects thinkr:PolarityType ;
    thinkr:revisionDate "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    thinkr:revisionKind thinkr:RevisionKindType.InitialBuild ;
    thinkr:revisionNote "First red-team pass, at MJSullivan's request, over the 36 Schmachtenberger-Hagens complements bridges, looking in the graph's own episode records for evidence against each. Added 2 Contests (SensemakingPrerequisiteOfOpenSociety_SharedBroadcastPerturbation, PowerSeekingAndComplicity_EducatingHyperAgents) and 3 of a new polarity, thinkr:PolarityType.Qualifies (MaximizingReturnsOnPower_MaximumPowerPrinciple, ImpossibleToHard_AggregateProbability, ImpossibleToHard_WhatCantWontMightHappen). Qualifies was added because Contests is all-or-nothing: one Curated Contests makes a link Disputed, which overstates a difference in emphasis. The other 31 bridges: no counter-evidence found in the graph's records. All new evidence is Candidate, so no calculatedConfidence changes until review; scripts/compute_confidence.py should ignore Qualifies as it ignores Mentions. Evidence IRIs name the LinkNote plus the source episode (e.g. tgs:Evidence.PowerSeekingAndComplicity_EducatingHyperAgents_Frankly_85), never the polarity, at MJSullivan's direction: polarity is a reviewable judgment that can change, the source cannot."@en ;
    .

tgs:RevisionEvent.EvidenceCitesEpisode_2026_10_19 a thinkr:RevisionEvent ;
    thinkr:affects thinkr:Evidence ;
    thinkr:revisionDate "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    thinkr:revisionKind thinkr:RevisionKindType.InitialBuild ;
    thinkr:revisionNote "Minted thinkr:citesEpisode (Evidence to Episode) at MJSullivan's request and backfilled it on every Evidence whose description names an episode (TGS_n, Frankly_n or RR_n): 44 Evidence individuals, 85 links, all resolved to existing episode IRIs with no ambiguity. The 23 Evidence individuals without one cite books, papers or historical figures, not episodes. New Evidence should set citesEpisode whenever its description names an episode."@en ;
    .

tgs:RevisionEvent.TGS_116_FullBuild a thinkr:RevisionEvent ;
    thinkr:affects tgs:Interview.TGS_116_RianeEisler, tgs:Human.RianeEisler ;
    thinkr:revisionDate "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    thinkr:revisionKind thinkr:RevisionKindType.InitialBuild ;
    thinkr:revisionNote "Built TGS_116 (Riane Eisler) from the transcript and show notes MJSullivan supplied, replacing the 2026-09-12 stub; closes the gap found when matching the Organism.earth author list (a TGS guest with no Human). New: Human, Persona and Relationship for Eisler; tgs:Organization.CenterForPartnershipSystems; six concepts (DominationPartnershipContinuum, FourCornerstonesOfPartnership, ChaliceAndBladePower, CaringEconomics, DenialLearnedInDominationFamilies, Pragmatopia); one convergence LinkNote (ChaliceAndBladePower with Nate's PowerVersusLife). Her three books now carry dct:creator and show-notes confirmation; MultilevelSelection gains her critique; TGS_56 gains a back-link."@en ;
    .

tgs:RevisionEvent.OppositionSources_2026_10_19 a thinkr:RevisionEvent ;
    thinkr:affects tgs:SchoolOfThought.TechnoOptimism, tgs:SchoolOfThought.Ecosocialism, tgs:SchoolOfThought.NeoclassicalGrowthEconomics ;
    thinkr:revisionDate "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    thinkr:revisionKind thinkr:RevisionKindType.InitialBuild ;
    thinkr:revisionNote "Second pass on opposition sources, at MJSullivan's request, after reviewing a second Gemini list. Added four works: Diesendorf and Wiedmann 2024 (peer-reviewed critique OF neoclassical economics, on TGS's side despite Gemini's framing), Duran's The Nerd Reich (2026; critic's account of the tech-billionaire network, linked to tgs:Work.TheSovereignIndividual), and two Monthly Review articles MJSullivan supplied as PDFs: Kolasi 2019 (ecosocialist; agrees with TGS on the biophysical diagnosis, differs on remedy, so no challenges link) and Hart-Landsberg 2026 (tech billionaires and AI). Hart-Landsberg's verbatim quote of the Techno-Optimist Manifesto's enemy list confirmed that it names 'the limits of growth' and the 'Precautionary Principle', so tgs:SchoolOfThought.TechnoOptimism now also challenges tgs:Concept.LimitsToGrowth and tgs:Concept.PrecautionaryPrinciple. Rejected from Gemini's list: Zero to One and Reentry (Gemini's glosses not supported by the books' subjects) and an unverifiable Knowledge International Journal paper."@en ;
    .

tgs:RevisionEvent.OstromCommons_2026_10_19 a thinkr:RevisionEvent ;
    thinkr:affects tgs:Concept.TragedyOfTheCommons, tgs:Concept.OstromDesignPrinciples ;
    thinkr:revisionDate "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    thinkr:revisionKind thinkr:RevisionKindType.InitialBuild ;
    thinkr:revisionNote "At MJSullivan's request, added Elinor Ostrom's work as the counterpoint to Hardin's tragedy of the commons: tgs:Concept.OstromDesignPrinciples (contrastsWith tgs:Concept.TragedyOfTheCommons), tgs:Work.GoverningTheCommons (1990) and tgs:Work.BeyondMarketsAndStates (Nobel lecture, 2009/2010). Prompted by a secondary explainer (Collison, ideasthesia, February 2026), cited in the concept's scopeNote only. Framed as a qualification rather than a refutation: Hardin's model holds for ungoverned open access, which Hardin himself later accepted. Frankly_108, which discusses Ostrom's monitoring and sanctioning research, now discusses the concept and references the book; the Bioregioning practice term Commons Governance Protocols now relatedMatches it."@en ;
    .

tgs:RevisionEvent.OneEarthSolutions_Import a thinkr:RevisionEvent ;
    thinkr:affects tgs:Work.OneEarthSolutions ;
    thinkr:revisionDate "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    thinkr:revisionKind thinkr:RevisionKindType.InitialBuild ;
    thinkr:revisionNote "Imported One Earth's solutions taxonomy at MJSullivan's request (solutions.ttl): 5 PracticeClusters (3 pillars, Levers of Change, Intersectional Themes), 12 sub-pillars, 76 solutions, 7 levers and 7 themes as PracticeTerms, with a Six Fronts crosswalk (skos:relatedMatch) set mostly at sub-pillar level. Definitions are Claude's paraphrases of One Earth's page. The energy pillar carries MJSullivan's and Nate's caveat that renewables are important but not enough by themselves; Energy Efficiency carries a Jevons caveat. The import gives first coverage to several Six Fronts subdomains Bioregioning Earth left empty (Transportation and Logistics, Plastic and Chemical Hazards, Non-Climate Planetary Boundaries, Anti-Corruption Infrastructure)."@en ;
    .

tgs:RevisionEvent.OneEarthBioregions2023_Import a thinkr:RevisionEvent ;
    thinkr:affects tgs:Work.OneEarthBioregions2023, thinkr:Bioregion ;
    thinkr:revisionDate "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    thinkr:revisionKind thinkr:RevisionKindType.InitialBuild ;
    thinkr:revisionNote "Imported One Earth's Bioregions 2023 framework at MJSullivan's request, with attribution (CC BY-NC 4.0, One Earth / Karl Burkart): bioregions.ttl holds 8 BiogeographicRealms, 14 BioregionalRealms, 53 BioregionalSubrealms and 185 Bioregions (codes as skos:notation). New classes and thinkr:inBioregion in tgs-core; tgs:Concept.Bioregion; the 2017 Dinerstein ecoregions paper as the source layer. Sources reconciled: names from One Earth's bioregion list, membership from the datahub CSV, subrealm names and realm grouping from the 2023 page (the CSV's realm column disagrees for four Palearctic subrealms; the page's grouping reproduces its stated counts exactly; the CSV's separate 'Alaskan Tundra' subrealm folded into Alaska). Sixteen Bioregioning Earth organizations whose places clearly fall in one bioregion were given thinkr:inBioregion (Claude's assignments from their placeName, for review); multi-bioregion or uncertain ones were left out."@en ;
    .

tgs:RevisionEvent.SKOSSchemes_2026_10_20 a thinkr:RevisionEvent ;
    thinkr:affects tgs:ConceptScheme.BioregioningEarth, tgs:ConceptScheme.OneEarthSolutions, tgs:ConceptScheme.OneEarthBioregions2023, tgs:ConceptScheme.SixFrontsOfIntervention ;
    thinkr:revisionDate "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    thinkr:revisionKind thinkr:RevisionKindType.InitialBuild ;
    thinkr:revisionNote "At MJSullivan's request, brought the imported taxonomies up to SKOS best practice for sharing: four skos:ConceptScheme individuals (Bioregioning Earth, One Earth Solutions, One Earth Bioregions 2023, and Nate's Six Fronts of Intervention), skos:inScheme on every member, skos:hasTopConcept / skos:topConceptOf on the roots, and the eight taxonomy classes made rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept, following the precedent of the subject schemes in subjects.ttl. The Six Fronts subdomains gain explicit skos:broader to their front (alongside thinkr:hasSubdomain) so plain SKOS tools see the hierarchy. One mapping that pointed at a SchoolOfThought (Doughnut Assessment) became rdfs:seeAlso, so skos:relatedMatch links concepts only. Also: the six TGS site subjects now carry skos:topConceptOf / skos:hasTopConcept; three One Earth subrealms that share their single bioregion's name (New Zealand, Greenland, Canadian Tundra) get 'Subrealm' appended to their prefLabel so labels are unique in the scheme. Left as designed: the MJSullivan-derived subtopics' skos:broader into the site-subjects scheme (a deliberate cross-scheme extension). Applied by applySkos.py, which should be re-run after regenerating any of these files."@en ;
    .

tgs:RevisionEvent.SKOSSchemes2_2026_10_20 a thinkr:RevisionEvent ;
    thinkr:affects tgs:ConceptScheme.TGSConcepts, tgs:ConceptScheme.CaliforniaDoughnutIndicators, tgs:ConceptScheme.EarthSystemComponents, tgs:ConceptScheme.SchoolsOfThought ;
    thinkr:revisionDate "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    thinkr:revisionKind thinkr:RevisionKindType.InitialBuild ;
    thinkr:revisionNote "Second SKOS pass, at MJSullivan's direction, so the whole graph can be shared as SKOS. Four more schemes: TGS Concepts (flat; every member a top concept), California Doughnut Indicators (2 halves > 21 categories > 42 indicators, via new skos:broader from hasDoughnutHalf / hasIndicatorCategory), Earth System Components, and Schools of Thought. At MJSullivan's correction, third-party classes stop being TGS concepts: thinkr:EarthSystemComponent, thinkr:IndicatorCategory and thinkr:Indicator are now rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept instead of thinkr:Concept, and their members lose explicit thinkr:Concept typing (matching the EarthSystemComponent class's own original rationale); thinkr:SchoolOfThought and thinkr:DoughnutHalf also become skos:Concept subclasses; thinkr:hasAlternateTerm's domain widened from thinkr:Concept to skos:Concept. Browsing collections: Nate's own concepts (thinkr:HagensConcept), one per TGS site subject, one per analytical lens. skos:related (within a scheme; skos:relatedMatch for the 10 pairs that cross schemes) materialized for concept-to-concept pairs of complements/contrastsWith/convergesWith/relatesTo/challenges (not as a subproperty axiom, since those properties also reach Personas, Organizations and ScenarioFacets). Plain skos:altLabel added from the 8 ExactMatch and Abbreviation alternate terms (applyAlt.py). Concept.CrudeOil's cross-scheme skos:broader to Subject.EnergySystems dropped (its dcterms:subject already says the same)."@en ;
    .

tgs:RevisionEvent.BioregioningOneEarthCrosswalk_2026_10_20 a thinkr:RevisionEvent ;
    thinkr:affects tgs:ConceptScheme.BioregioningEarth, tgs:ConceptScheme.OneEarthSolutions ;
    thinkr:revisionDate "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    thinkr:revisionKind thinkr:RevisionKindType.InitialBuild ;
    thinkr:revisionNote "Added 40 direct SKOS mappings from Bioregioning Earth practice terms to One Earth Solutions terms (closeMatch, narrowMatch, relatedMatch, broadMatch; no exactMatch, which is transitive and claims more than either source supports), so WWNS can go from a solution type straight to the initiatives practicing it. Claude's first-pass draft, accepted by MJSullivan as a starting point to enrich later. Deliberately unmatched: Species Control, Interspecies Mutualism, Disaster Relief, Coaches and Leaders."@en ;
    .

tgs:RevisionEvent.Frankly_76_FullBuild a thinkr:RevisionEvent ;
    thinkr:affects tgs:Monologue.Frankly_76_TheBattlesOfOurTime ;
    thinkr:revisionDate "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    thinkr:revisionKind thinkr:RevisionKindType.InitialBuild ;
    thinkr:revisionNote "Full build from the official transcript and show notes, replacing the 2026-09-12 stub. Minted tgs:Concept.BattlesOfOurTime and tgs:Concept.Effectivism, added to the TGS Concepts scheme and their collections, with skos:related links. Notes added to tgs:Concept.PowerVersusLife and tgs:Concept.CulturalMitochondria, which this Frankly anticipates. Back-links on all three references."@en ;
    .

tgs:RevisionEvent.Frankly_70_FullBuild a thinkr:RevisionEvent ;
    thinkr:affects tgs:Monologue.Frankly_70_AskMeAnything ;
    thinkr:revisionDate "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    thinkr:revisionKind thinkr:RevisionKindType.InitialBuild ;
